% TRXViz citation database.
%
% This file is the single source of truth for every reference used by
% both the TRXViz documentation (via mkdocs-bibtex) and the runtime
% methods-boilerplate generator (see `workflow::methods`).
%
% Conventions:
%   - Entry keys are lowercase, no year suffix unless needed for
%     disambiguation (`dipy`, `purifibre`, `yeh2013gqi`).
%   - Keep one blank line between entries for readability.
%   - Runtime code references these keys via `WorkflowOp::citation_keys`;
%     docs reference them with Pandoc syntax (e.g. a Pandoc citation to
%     the 'dipy' key).
%   - Any op that re-implements or ports a published method MUST add a
%     citation here rather than embedding prose in code.
%   - Keep this list conservative: cite only methods whose behavior is
%     materially represented in TRXViz, so users can credit authors
%     accurately. Do not add "nice to have" or tangentially-related
%     work — they clutter generated methods sections.
%
% IMPORTANT: The presence of a citation here does NOT mean the cited
% authors have reviewed, contributed to, or endorsed TRXViz. See
% `NON_ENDORSEMENT_NOTICE` in `workflow::methods` for the full text.

